From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] style: load user themes above the built-in base

A user theme's singularity/style.css is loaded at
GTK_STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_APPLICATION + 5 and its dark/light variant at
+ 6, which is BELOW the built-in libsingularity base palette at
GTK_STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_USER (800). The theme template documents that
"this file is loaded above the built-in libsingularity base, so any rule
here overrides the default Singularity look", but at the current
priorities a theme can only ADD properties and use its own named colors;
it cannot override a base named color (@window_bg, @surface_bg,
@text_color, ...) or any property the base already sets, because a named
color resolves from the highest-priority provider that defines it.

Load the user theme at USER + 3 and its variant at USER + 4, above the
base/accent/recolor providers, so a theme can also opt into overriding
named colors and base properties, as documented. Themes that only derive
from @accent_color are unaffected (a higher priority does not change what
a rule that already wins paints).

Not filed upstream by this task: the same change is proposed to Mirko
Brombin (upstream maintainer); carried here as an NCZ overlay patch until
it lands upstream.
---
 src/style/style_manager.vala | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/style/style_manager.vala b/src/style/style_manager.vala
index 0976170..5139330 100644
--- a/src/style/style_manager.vala
+++ b/src/style/style_manager.vala
@@ -766,9 +766,11 @@ namespace Singularity.Style {
          *
          * Searches standard theme directories for a directory named
          * `theme_name` containing `singularity/style.css`.  The CSS is loaded
-         * at priority 605 (above the built-in base at 600).  If the theme also
-         * provides `singularity/style-light.css` it will be swapped in/out when
-         * apply_color_scheme is called.
+         * at priority GTK_STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_USER + 3 (803), above the
+         * built-in base at USER (800), so the theme can override base named
+         * colours and properties as the theme template documents.  If the theme
+         * also provides `singularity/style-light.css` it will be swapped in/out
+         * when apply_color_scheme is called (at USER + 4).
          *
          * Pass an empty string to unload any previously loaded user theme and
          * revert to the built-in default look.
@@ -806,7 +808,7 @@ namespace Singularity.Style {
                 StyleContext.add_provider_for_display(
                     Gdk.Display.get_default(),
                     user_theme_provider,
-                    Gtk.STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_APPLICATION + 5
+                    Gtk.STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_USER + 3
                 );
             } catch (Error e) {
                 warning("StyleManager: failed to load user theme '%s': %s", theme_name, e.message);
@@ -837,7 +839,7 @@ namespace Singularity.Style {
                 StyleContext.add_provider_for_display(
                     Gdk.Display.get_default(),
                     user_theme_variant_provider,
-                    Gtk.STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_APPLICATION + 6
+                    Gtk.STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_USER + 4
                 );
             } catch (Error e) {
                 warning("StyleManager: failed to load user theme variant: %s", e.message);
-- 
